 a new branch, CI passed, and the pull request against main is open with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even` (commit `08d3cd5986`), I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **Pull request:** The request to open it timed out. Before retrying, I checked and found it had been created as PR #101, but without alex as a reviewer, so I added him to it rather than opening a second one.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool didn't recognise that ID. I went by the test and the docstring, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged. That needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QfMTHYMmFRYRCQyy3k5kyp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WFR77WD5Tq7NnebFkPSjRk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017kBJNnGsQNYANKq8c2jnvu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Qg9zYuBeNBpYH6WVFGxY6i", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Fna7gvADnB4cZQJXWFsvJ6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "fi